=== ffm backup target
Usage:
  ffm backup target [flags]
  ffm backup target [command]

Available Commands:
  add         Add a target; it is tested (write, list, read, delete) before it is saved
  list        List backup targets (no secrets)
  remove      Forget a target (archives stored on it are left alone)
  test        Write, list, read back and delete a small object on a target

Global Flags:
      --non-interactive   Never open interactive prompts; fail with a message naming the missing flag instead. Implied when $CI or $FFM_NON_INTERACTIVE is set, or when there is no controlling terminal (set $FFM_INTERACTIVE=1 to force prompting back on)
      --verbose           Show docker compose output

Use "ffm backup target [command] --help" for more information about a command.

=== ffm backup target add
Usage:
  ffm backup target add <name> [flags]

Examples:
  echo "$SECRET" | ffm backup target add r2 --type s3 --endpoint <account>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com \
      --bucket backups --access-key-id <id> --secret-access-key-stdin
  ffm backup target add box --type sftp --host backup.example.com --user ffm \
      --key-file ~/.ssh/ffm_backup --path /backups --accept-host-key
  ffm backup target add nas --type local --path /mnt/nas/ffm
  ffm backup target add drive --type rclone --remote gdrive:ffm-backups

Flags:
      --accept-host-key                 sftp: fetch the server's host key now and pin it
      --access-key-id string            s3: access key id
      --bucket string                   s3: bucket (must exist)
      --endpoint string                 s3: endpoint host, e.g. s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com
      --host string                     sftp: server
      --host-key string                 sftp: the server's host key, as one line of ssh-keyscan output without the host
      --insecure                        s3: plain HTTP (a MinIO on a private network)
      --key-file string                 sftp: private key file (no passphrase; use a dedicated key)
      --no-test                         Save without testing the target
      --path string                     sftp: directory on the server; local: absolute directory
      --port int                        sftp: port (default 22)
      --prefix string                   Folder inside the target for ffm's archives
      --region string                   s3: region, when the provider needs one
      --remote string                   rclone: remote and path, e.g. gdrive:ffm (configured with rclone config)
      --replace                         Replace a target with the same name
      --secret-access-key-file string   s3: read the secret access key from this file at each use
      --secret-access-key-stdin         s3: read the secret access key from stdin
      --type string                     s3, sftp, local or rclone
      --user string                     sftp: user

Global Flags:
      --non-interactive   Never open interactive prompts; fail with a message naming the missing flag instead. Implied when $CI or $FFM_NON_INTERACTIVE is set, or when there is no controlling terminal (set $FFM_INTERACTIVE=1 to force prompting back on)
      --verbose           Show docker compose output

