=== ffm backup verify
Usage:
  ffm backup verify [archive] [flags]

Examples:
  ffm backup verify ~/frappe/_backups/mybench/mybench_20261008T120000Z.ffm.tar
  ffm backup verify mybench_….ffm.tar.age --identity ~/ffm-backup.key --restore
  ffm backup verify --target r2 --bench mybench --identity ~/ffm-backup.key

Flags:
      --bench string      Bench whose archive --target verifies
      --identity string   age identity file for an encrypted archive. Env: FFM_AGE_IDENTITY_FILE
      --json              Print the result as JSON (schema ffm.verify/v1)
      --notify            Report the result through 'ffm notify' notifiers (for a cron job)
      --restore           Also restore into a throwaway bench, ping its site, and delete it
      --target string     Verify the newest archive on this backup target (needs --bench)

Global Flags:
      --non-interactive   Never open interactive prompts; fail with a message naming the missing flag instead. Implied when $CI or $FFM_NON_INTERACTIVE is set, or when there is no controlling terminal (set $FFM_INTERACTIVE=1 to force prompting back on)
      --verbose           Show docker compose output

