=== ffm create
Usage:
  ffm create <name> [flags]

Flags:
      --acme-email string            Email for Let's Encrypt certificates (required on first --mode prod bench with SSL)
      --admin-password string        Frappe site admin password (default "admin")
      --agent                        Agent-ready dev bench: ports on 127.0.0.1, no SSH agent, a random admin password unless you set one, and ffc/MCP acting as a dedicated System Manager user (agent@<site>) instead of Administrator
      --agent-read-only              Like --agent, with the MCP server limited to read tools
      --alias-tls                    Serve --domain-alias names over HTTPS with Let's Encrypt instead of plain HTTP. Production with SSL only; every alias must be publicly resolvable.
      --apps stringArray             Apps to install: short name (erpnext), URL (git@github.com:org/app.git), or URL@branch
      --db-password string           Database root password (default "ffm123456")
      --db-type string               Database engine: mariadb or postgres (default "mariadb")
      --domain string                Public domain for production (required for --mode prod), e.g. erp.example.com
      --domain-alias stringArray     Extra hostname the bench also answers on, e.g. erp.internal. Repeatable. Requires the shared proxy ('ffm proxy start') and DNS pointing the name at this host. Same as 'ffm domain add' after creation.
      --frappe-branch string         Frappe branch (version-16 or version-15) (default "version-16")
      --frappe-repo string           Custom Frappe repository URL with optional @branch suffix (e.g. https://github.com/your-org/frappe.git@main). Defaults to the official frappe/frappe repo.
      --github-token string          GitHub personal access token for private HTTPS repos
      --gunicorn-workers int         Number of gunicorn worker processes (prod only). Rule of thumb: 2*CPU+1. (default 2)
      --keep-on-failure              On failure, leave containers and the bench directory in place instead of rolling back, so logs survive for diagnosis. Env: FFM_KEEP_ON_FAILURE
      --lan                          Publish the bench's ports on all interfaces instead of 127.0.0.1 (needed to reach it from another machine, and for dev domain aliases). Refused with the default admin password
      --mariadb-buffer-pool string   InnoDB buffer pool size for MariaDB (e.g. 512M, 1G, 2G, 4G). Prod only; dev uses 256M. (default "1G")
      --mariadb-fast-commit          Prod + MariaDB: innodb_flush_log_at_trx_commit=2, faster commits that a crash can lose up to about a second of. The default (1) loses none
      --match-host-user              Build the image with the container's frappe user remapped to your uid/gid. Needed wherever your uid is not 1000 (e.g. GitHub-hosted runners, uid 1001), otherwise the ./workspace bind mount is unwritable from one side. Env: FFM_MATCH_HOST_USER
      --mode string                  Bench mode: dev or prod (default "dev")
      --no-seed                      Run bench init, get-app and bench build from the branch heads instead of copying a seed, and do not save one. Env: FFM_NO_SEED
      --no-ssl                       Skip Let's Encrypt SSL in production (handle TLS externally via Caddy/Nginx)
      --node string                  Node major version: 22 or 24. Default: 22 for version-15, 24 otherwise
      --proxy-host string            Public domain for reverse proxy, e.g. frappe.example.com (sets per-site host_name)
      --proxy-port int               Configure for reverse proxy: set socketio_port to this value (e.g. 443 for HTTPS, 80 for HTTP)
      --python string                Python version for the bench virtualenv: 3.12 or 3.14. Default: 3.12 for version-15, 3.14 otherwise
      --redis-cache-maxmem string    Redis cache maxmemory limit (e.g. 256mb, 512mb, 1gb). Uses allkeys-lru eviction. (default "512mb")
      --redis-queue-maxmem string    Redis queue maxmemory limit. Uses noeviction so jobs are never silently dropped. (default "512mb")
      --slow-query-log               Enable MariaDB slow query log (threshold: 2s). Writes to <bench>/mysql-logs/. Prod + MariaDB only.
      --socketio-port int            Fixed host Socket.IO port. Must equal --web-port + 1000.
      --ssh-agent                    Forward the host SSH agent into the dev frappe container, for SSH-URL private repos. Requires SSH_AUTH_SOCK
      --web-port int                 Fixed host web port instead of auto-allocating from 8000. Must be paired with --socketio-port (= web port + 1000). Each bench publishes a 6-port range, so parallel benches must be at least 10 apart.
      --worker-long-replicas int     Number of long-queue background worker replicas (prod only). (default 1)
      --worker-short-replicas int    Number of short-queue background worker replicas (prod only). (default 1)

Global Flags:
      --non-interactive   Never open interactive prompts; fail with a message naming the missing flag instead. Implied when $CI or $FFM_NON_INTERACTIVE is set, or when there is no controlling terminal (set $FFM_INTERACTIVE=1 to force prompting back on)
      --verbose           Show docker compose output

