=== ffm restore
Usage:
  ffm restore <archive> [name] [flags]

Examples:
  ffm restore ~/frappe/_backups/mybench/mybench_20260826T090000Z.ffm.tar
  ffm restore mybench_20260826T090000Z.ffm.tar staging
  ffm restore mybench_20260826T090000Z.ffm.tar --dry-run
  ffm restore prod_20260826T090000Z.ffm.tar --domain erp.example.com --pin-apps
  ffm restore mybench_20260826T090000Z.ffm.tar --app my_app=git@github.com:acme/my_app.git@main

Flags:
      --acme-email string              Let's Encrypt account address for a production restore
      --admin-password string          Set a new Administrator password instead of keeping the archived one
      --allow-missing-encryption-key   Restore even though the archive has no site encryption key, accepting that Password fields (email passwords, integration secrets) will not decrypt
      --app stringArray                Clone an app from this source instead: <app>=<git-url>[@branch] (repeatable; frappe=... sets the framework's repo)
      --domain string                  Override the production domain recorded in the archive
      --dry-run                        Validate the archive and print the plan without creating anything
      --encryption-key string          Key for a GPG-encrypted database dump, when the archive does not carry it
      --github-token string            GitHub token for cloning private apps; github.com SSH sources are cloned over HTTPS with it
      --identity string                age identity file that decrypts an encrypted (.age) archive. Env: FFM_AGE_IDENTITY_FILE
      --keep-on-failure                Leave a failed restore in place for diagnosis instead of removing it
      --lan                            Publish the bench's ports on all interfaces instead of 127.0.0.1 (needed to reach it from another machine, and for dev domain aliases). Refused with the default admin password
      --no-files                       Restore the database only, without attachments
      --no-ssl                         Serve the restored production bench over plain HTTP
      --pin-apps                       Check each app out at the commit recorded in the archive instead of its branch head
      --reallocate-ports               Always assign a fresh port pair instead of reusing the archive's
      --skip-migrate                   Skip 'bench migrate' after restoring — only safe when the apps are at the backed-up versions
      --skip-space-check               Restore without checking free disk space first
      --socketio-port int              Explicit host Socket.IO port
      --ssh-agent                      Forward the host SSH agent into the dev frappe container, for SSH-URL private repos. Requires SSH_AUTH_SOCK
      --web-port int                   Explicit host web port

Global Flags:
      --non-interactive   Never open interactive prompts; fail with a message naming the missing flag instead. Implied when $CI or $FFM_NON_INTERACTIVE is set, or when there is no controlling terminal (set $FFM_INTERACTIVE=1 to force prompting back on)
      --verbose           Show docker compose output

